{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nWe arrived in Giessen this morning. The professors here are charming, and the wine excellent. I spent the afternoon in lively debate with the theologians, which was most invigorating. We are now traveling down the Lahn with a young schoolteacher. The river is calm, the air fresh.\n\nI passed Weilburg this evening. It is a fine, quiet place, formerly a princely residence. I find myself thinking of our home in Berlin. The distance feels greater when one is moving. I hope the children are well and that Karl is applying himself to his studies. I shall be back before the month is out, I trust.\n\nDo not worry about me. The journey is pleasant. I have enough snuff and my books are secure.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080134,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":173,"prompt_tokens":944,"total_tokens":1117,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-HbH85TvaqwQQUR4D1NnMTxkhtxQWMM5X","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":944,"prompt_ms":911.824,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9659152542372881,"prompt_per_second":1035.2875116250505,"predicted_n":173,"predicted_ms":4155.288,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.158651162790694,"predicted_per_second":41.39303942350086}}